A||N||5||bHooper||need help with a salvage car seat thats stuck.||||1||
Z||000000||bHooper||05-30-2001||05:28 PM||||i'm working on a salvaged car that has it's window knocked out on the passenger side... thussly, the passenger seat is stuck in it's track (due to rust).  any thoughts on removal?  it doestn slide at all... even with a johnson bar's assistance!<P>thanks!<BR>hoop||||reg||1
Z||000001||tgowens||05-30-2001||05:33 PM||||hoop, get one of those flat 13mm ratchets (Sears has them and some of the auto parts stores carry them) you know the kind, 13mm on one end and something else on the other - looks like a dog bone.......slide that under the seat on the nut and ratchet them off.......<P>------------------<BR><A HREF="http://www.tgowens.com/fiero/index.html" TARGET=_blank><BR>                <IMG SRC="http://www.tgowens.com/fiero/3GTS_SIG.gif">                 </A>||||reg||1
Z||000002||bHooper||05-30-2001||05:46 PM||||i will try soething like that, however, one of theproblems with that is that the car has a busted windshield and there is glass everywhere.  i cut myself good, 3 times today!<P>hoop||||reg||1
Z||000003||gabriel||05-31-2001||02:13 PM||||Dude, a fairly common problem when the seat is stuck is not that the tracks are rusted together, but that the spring that connects the seat adjustment lever to the opposite side track release is rusted out. It's hard to see it without a mirror, but if you slide a long screwdriver or such under the seat and just put it between the release and the track, the seat will move free.  If you don't release it, all the prying in the world wont move the seat. ||||reg||1
Z||000004||theogre||05-31-2001||02:27 PM||||go to sears or someplace and get a nut splitter.... use it to break the nuts off. You'll be able to reach the splitter with an extension and socket even if it's under the seat. You might need a wobble end extension or a universal joint depending on how far under the seat you need to get...||||reg||1
Z||000005||bHooper||05-31-2001||05:42 PM||||you know, a night to think about it is often the best tool!<P>i put my 13mm wrench on the front nuts, took them off, pryed the seat up, then did the same thing on the rear... presto chango, no seato!<P>thanks guys!<P><P>------------------<BR>hoop<BR>Red '86 GT 5 speed<BR>*Black '86 SE Automatic||||reg||1
